    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "MESABA AIRLINES\nSafety Information\nRJ-85\nNORTHWEST\nFederal regulations require all passengers to review this important information, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, illuminated cabin signs, posted placards, and oral directions and hand signals\ngiven by crew members.\nKnow the location and operation of all emergency equipment and exits.\nIn an emergency evacuation, if a crew member cannot reach an exit near you, you may have to open it.\nONLY open the exit after the plane has completely come to a stop.\nLook outside: If fire, smoke, or water could come in through the exit, do not open it, direct passengers to\nusable exits.\nIf it is safe to open the exit, open it quickly and clear a pathway in the row.to the exit.\nShout \"Open seatbelts!\",\n\", \"Come this way!\" and exit the airplane as quickly as possible.\nHelp other passengers out of the airplane, if there is no immediate danger.\nDirect passengers to a safe path away and quickly get yourself clear of the airplane.\nWhen finished reviewing this card please return it to the seat pocket for our next customer.\nOrig. 4/97",
      "Bracing\npositions\nEmergency exits\nKnow the location and\noperation of all exits\nUsing the exits, quickly\nevacuate the aircraft.\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow to check outside\nfor the following:\nSmoke\nIf smoke is so thick you\ncan not see out, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nFire\nIf there is fire outside\nthe aircraft, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nDebris\nIf there is metal debris or\nobstructions, redirect\npassengers to other exits.\nA\nOxygen\nA\nFollo: lights to exits\nA\nB\nUse handles to stabilize slide.\nCheck that the slide has inflated\nand is in good condition.\nCheck that the slide has inflated\nand is in good condition.\nUse handles to stabilize slide.",
      "Flotation Cushion\n2\nIn water use rear exits\nonly on crew command\nCopyright © Aero Safety Graphics Inc., 1997. All Rights Reserved. Printed in USA. Tel: (800) 376-4622, Fax: (206) 868-9017"
    ],
